# Trust the LIO MORE: one variable changed, and its two couplings handled explicitly.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS.  `params/ekf_trust_lio.parm` is FROZEN (frozen/mission_a.manifest:56,
# sha 4f3d4ff0...) because every accepted A/B/C row in docs/metrics/ was flown with it.  This file is a
# COPY of it with ONE physical change, selected per-run with `EKF_PARM=`, so both configurations stay on
# the record and the frozen set stays byte-for-byte intact.
#
# THE MEASUREMENT THAT MOTIVATES IT (2026-10-16).  The FCU's own estimate (XKF1 in the flight log) sits
# 16.2-21.2 mm RMS from the truth tap horizontally and 29.0-44.6 mm vertically, while the LIO it is fed is
# 3.38-4.57 mm from the same truth (A1) -- a factor of 4-5.  It is NOT lag: best-fit lag is +2..+20 ms and
# the residual barely moves at zero lag (e.g. RECT7 17.93 -> 17.92 mm).  It is the noise the filter is TOLD.
#
# WHICH PARAMETER ACTUALLY CARRIES THAT NOISE (read from the source, not assumed):
#   * `EK3_POSNE_M_NSE` is `_gpsHorizPosNoise` (libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3.cpp:184) and
#     `EK3_VELNE_M_NSE`/`EK3_ALT_M_NSE` are the GPS velocity and BARO altitude noises.  With
#     `EK3_SRC1_POSXY/POSZ/VELXY/VELZ/YAW = 6` (ExternalNav) no GPS is fused, so those three are INERT here.
#   * `VISO_TYPE 1` selects the MAVLink vision backend, and
#     `libraries/AP_VisualOdom/AP_VisualOdom_MAV.cpp:42` does
#     `posErr = constrain_float(posErr, _frontend.get_pos_noise(), 100.0f)` -- i.e. **VISO_POS_M_NSE is a
#     FLOOR** for the position noise.  Our ODOMETRY sends zero covariances
#     (`bridge/mavlink_impl.py:442-449`, `[0.0]*21, [0.0]*21`), so the message declares no error and the
#     floor is what the EKF uses.  The flight log proves it: `PErr` is a constant 30.00 mm = the old 0.03,
#     `VErr` a constant 30.00 mm/s = VISO_VEL_M_NSE (direct, :79), `AErr` a constant 20.00 mrad = the old
#     0.02.  Code and log agree, so this is not an inference.
#
# THE ONE CHANGE: VISO_POS_M_NSE 0.03 -> 0.01 (30 mm -> 10 mm).  The measured error is 3.4-4.6 mm, so
# 10 mm is still 2x-3x conservative -- deliberately: this is the first step, not the limit.
#
# ITS TWO COUPLINGS, BOTH HANDLED (the frozen file documents what happens when they are not:
# "with 3.0 the tolerance was 90 mm and a normal trajectory-following manoeuvre tripped it -- 3 of 5
# Mission B flights ended in LAND mode", EKF failsafe, not the estimator, was the problem):
#   1. FS_EKF_THRESH is compared against the innovation consistency TEST RATIO
#      (`AP_AHRS::get_variances` -> `NavEKF3::getVariances`, "return the innovation consistency test
#      ratios", libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3.cpp:1532), which scales as 1/assumed-noise.  Shrinking the
#      position noise 3x inflates the ratio 3x, so the threshold moves 3x with it (10.0 -> 30.0) and the
#      ABSOLUTE tolerance stays where the frozen file put it (~300 mm: 0.300 / 0.01 = 30).
#   2. `EK3_POS_I_GATE` is "the percentage number of standard deviations ... applied to the position
#      measurement innovation consistency check" (AP_NavEKF3.cpp:186-192, 500 = 5.00 SD), so it too is in
#      units of the assumed noise: 5 SD x 30 mm was 150 mm absolute, 5 SD x 10 mm would be 50 mm -- 3x
#      TIGHTER in metres, which is how good measurements start getting rejected.  It is therefore raised
#      by the same 3x (500 -> 1500) so the gate stays at 150 mm absolute.  The acceptance check for this
#      is `Ign` in the VISP/VISV log records, which was 0 of 2632 on the reference flight: if it becomes
#      non-zero, the tighter configuration is throwing good measurements away and has FAILED.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED IN THIS FILE: VISO_VEL_M_NSE.  The velocity the EKF receives is a STAIRCASE --
# measured from RECT7's own log: 48.40 Hz delivery but only 10.08 DISTINCT values/s (the 10 Hz
# /lio/odom source held into a 48 Hz stream), steps at each change median 10.41 mm/s, p90 134.73,
# max 287.28 mm/s -- so its honest noise is LARGER than 0.03, not smaller, and that is the next
# experiment, on its own, so that this one stays attributable.  Also unchanged: VISO_YAW_M_NSE (EKF3
# floors the yaw error at 5 deg = 87 mrad anyway, AP_NavEKF3_Measurements.cpp:1129), and the EK3_* noise
# entries, which are inert here for the reason above.
EK3_POSNE_M_NSE 0.03
EK3_VELNE_M_NSE 0.03
EK3_VELD_M_NSE 0.05
EK3_ALT_M_NSE 0.10
EK3_YAW_M_NSE 0.02
VISO_POS_M_NSE 0.01
VISO_VEL_M_NSE 0.03
VISO_YAW_M_NSE 0.02
EK3_ACC_P_NSE 0.10
EK3_GYRO_P_NSE 0.003
EK3_ABIAS_P_NSE 0.002
EK3_GBIAS_P_NSE 0.0002
EK3_POS_I_GATE 1500
FS_EKF_THRESH 30.0
